### Semantic HTML

#### Definition with examples and motivation

Give a few examples of semantic HTML elements and explain why this is important. Answer in your own words.

#### Website without CSS

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('html-without-css')} />

> **Most important takeaway (especially for digital humanities students):** “HTML tags must be used for their semantic value, not their appearance. It's always possible to totally change the look and feel of a given tag using CSS so, when using HTML, take the time to focus on the meaning rather than the appearance.” [Source: MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Cheatsheet)

**Bonus: Micro-project.** With only HTML (no CSS), try to replicate a layout and compare Firefox and Chrome. Use `section`, `aside`, `ul`, `li`, `h1`, `h2`, `h3`, `p`, `strong`, `em`, `del`, `ins`, `a`, `form`, `input`, and `button`.

**Bonus:** [Mark up dates and times](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Advanced_text_features#marking_up_times_and_dates)
